Dynamic Git to Azure Data Lake Pipeline (Azure Data Factory)

Pipeline Workflow (Step-by-Step)
Step 1: Create Linked Services

Created HTTP Linked Service to connect with GitHub raw files
Created Azure Data Lake Linked Service for storage

Step 2: Create Parameterized Source Dataset

Created a dataset for GitHub CSV files
Used dynamic parameter for relative URL
Enabled dynamic file selection

Step 3: Create Parameterized Sink Dataset

Created a dataset for Azure Data Lake
Used parameters for:
Folder name
File name
Configured Bronze layer storage path

Step 4: Build Lookup Activity

Added a Lookup activity to read metadata
Lookup returns a list of file paths to process
Acts as input for dynamic looping

Step 5: Implement ForEach Activity

Used ForEach activity to iterate over file list
Enables processing of multiple files dynamically

Step 6: Add Copy Data Activity

Placed inside ForEach loop
Copies data from GitHub to Data Lake
Uses dynamic dataset parameters

Step 7: Validate and Publish Pipeline

Validated pipeline configuration
Published changes in Azure Data Factory
